  "costs": [
    "Retain uses an atomic bounded-CAS loop and release uses an atomic decrement; no plain refcount reads remain.",
    "A warm builtin acquisition uses a short global slot lock and an atomic reference; Match still traverses UTF8/trie data.",
    "Cold competing builtin builders can duplicate CRC/trie/context allocations and work; unused candidates are destroyed outside the global spin.",
    "Add validates UTF8, computes C strlen once, copies the sequence/SVG, reserves metadata and publishes. Failed edits can retain reserved capacity, but cannot retain failed payloads or alter logical mappings.",
    "XRT counters do not measure all third-party/system allocations; no throughput/RSS/whole-binding zero-cost claim."
  ],
  "qualificationNotes": [
    "C11 O0/O2 and C++11/C++17 clients call actual host/static products. Aggregate tests separately exercise private invariants.",
    "Linux TSan instruments the aggregate and canonical XRT including allocator/locks/atomics; remaining archive objects are uninstrumented. UBSan instruments aggregate only.",
